    33	    losing a race: an unwritable claims dir, a missing `cortextos`, a timeout,
    34	    or any refusal whose stderr names no real claim verdict.
    35	
    36	    That distinction is load-bearing (G2A-3). `acquire` returning None means
    37	    "another LIVE run holds the claim", and the caller turns that into exit 2
    38	    with the success receipt left BYTE-IDENTICAL. Collapsing an operational
    39	    failure into the same None reported a poller that could not run at all as
    40	    ordinary contention, and the stale receipt kept the digest calm."""
    41	
    42	
    43	class LeaseLost(Exception):
    44	    """Raised by the caller when `Lease.lost` is set: the lock file this run
    45	    holds has disappeared (a concurrent stale-sweep, or another poller already
    46	    reclaimed it). Single-flight is no longer guaranteed, so the run must STOP
    47	    before any further effect rather than keep writing (G0B2-13)."""
