clientstate: key is written. Successful delivery precedes ledger persistence at client_state_gmail.py:365-383 and :649-671.","counterexample":"Telegram delivers an ambiguity alert, then the process dies before ledger.append. If the next poll occurs after the bus's six-hour content-dedup window, the unchanged message has no persisted escalation proof and is delivered again for the same source_ref/content_digest."},{"id":4,"verdict":"HOLDS","evidence":"scripts/brain/resolve_email.py:90-104 guards empty company values before _norm_title, rejects falsey duplicate-suppressed mappings, and queries domain_to_slug only with the full normalized domain. Unknown results become no-known-entity at :139-147.","counterexample":"none"},{"id":5,"verdict":"HOLDS","evidence":"scripts/brain/extract_email.py:55-68 and :264 use the exact required Claude argv; :211-233 schema/type-validates and range-checks matches_open_item; client_state_projections.py:84-93 routes created commitments through --assignee human --type human, while page and CRM projections omit commitments. Independent focused Python execution passed the argv, validation, cache, threshold, and projection checks.","counterexample":"none"},{"id":6,"verdict":"VIOLATED","evidence":"scripts/brain/client_state_gmail.py:531-574 otherwise limits auto-creation to the sender and writes one interaction per distinct contact effect. However, client_state_projections.py:62 substitutes from_email when the From display name is empty, so the persisted name fact is not from the display name required by FR-006.","counterexample":"A domain-matched message with `From: alice@acme.org` parses as from_name='' and from_email='alice@acme.org'. With no contact row, the system invokes upsert-contact.py with `--name alice@acme.org --email alice@acme.org`, manufacturing the name from the address."},{"id":7,"verdict":"HOLDS","evidence":"scripts/brain/client_state_gmail.py:303-319 preserves revision_of through partial and simulated rows; :590-612 previews without a vault mutation and performs live read-render-write under the page lock. scripts/brain/writeback_email.py:40-59 marks revisions and :87-124 preserves existing History content while appending the new entry.","counterexample":"none"},{"id":8,"verdict":"VIOLATED","evidence":"scripts/brain/client_state_writes.py:193-200 implements owner match plus ratio strictly greater than 0.75; :211-243 implements tier-2/tier-1 planning; client_state_projections.py:84-93 creates tasks with both human flags. But src/bus/task.ts:1161-1168 exempts claimants named human or user from the force requirement. The two targeted Vitest files passed 24/24, including tests that affirm this weaker bypass.","counterexample":"An autonomous caller runs `cortextos bus claim-task <human-task-id> --agent human` without --force-claim. src/cli/bus.ts:684-695 accepts the caller-supplied agent name, HUMAN_CLAIMANTS bypasses the guard, and claimTask succeeds."},{"id":9,"verdict":"HOLDS","evidence":"Reachable dry-run subprocesses are: meeting-brief-claim plus at most one stale-cleared retry (single_flight.py:205-221); the full gws gmail +triage query plus one per-day query when capped (gmail_source.py:292-323); gws gmail +read per listed message (:280-289); list-tasks for human and build per fileable message (client_state_writes.py:247-270); the exact Claude call on cache miss (extract_email.py:356-381); and meeting-brief-release (single_flight.py:69-92). Reachable writes are confined to --state-dir: directory creation, claim-file creation/touches/release, LoggingRunner argv.log, observations.jsonl, run-receipt.json, atomic temporary files, and applicable lock/failure diagnostics. client_state_gmail.py:540-574,591-603,633-650 skips CRM subprocesses, vault locks/page writes, create-task, and send-telegram in dry-run.","counterexample":"none"},{"id":10,"verdict":"HOLDS","evidence":"`git diff --diff-filter=M --name-only feature/client-state-gmail-v1...HEAD` returns exactly .gitignore, scripts/brain/meeting_loop_watch.py, src/bus/task.ts, and src/cli/bus.ts; .gitignore is +1/-0. All implementation/tests/ops artifacts outside those four are newly added files. Independent focused runs passed 24 Python pure tests and 24 TypeScript tests; tmp_path-dependent Python tests could not be independently executed in the read-only verifier sandbox because Python had no writable temporary directory.","counterexample":"none"}],"findings":[{"id":"G2B-1","severity":"Critical","title":"Failed model outputs are not covered by the at-most-once extraction identity","location":"scripts/brain/extract_email.py:264","evidence":"A successful Claude process can produce malformed or schema-invalid output at lines 268-271. No observation or attempted-identity marker is persisted before ExtractionError exits, so an unchanged retry invokes the model again.","fix":"Persist a durable extraction-attempt state keyed by source_ref/digest/bound slugs before invocation and prevent automatic re-invocation after an indeterminate or invalid result, or amend the binding guarantee to permit explicit retries."},{"id":"G2B-2","severity":"Critical","title":"Escalation delivery still lacks the mandatory clientstate send-side key","location":"scripts/brain/client_state_gmail.py:179","evidence":"The command is only `cortextos bus send-telegram <chat> <text>`. Ledger proof is written after delivery, leaving a crash window in which Telegram delivered but no dedup record exists; the projection comment at client_state_projections.py:100 confirms no clientstate: key is written.","fix":"Send with a stable clientstate:-namespaced source key derived from source_ref and content_digest, using the fail-closed comms/source-key path, while retaining the monotonic ledger record after confirmed delivery."},{"id":"G2B-3","severity":"Critical","title":"Missing display names are replaced with the email address as a contact name","location":"scripts/brain/client_state_projections.py:62","evidence":"`from_name or from_email` writes the address into the name field, contrary to the binding source mapping `{name}` from the From display name and `{email}` from the address.","fix":"Use a dedicated minimal-create path that may use the address for identity but persists the name exactly from the display-name field, including an explicit missing-name representation instead of synthesizing a name."},{"id":"G2B-4","severity":"Critical","title":"Caller-controlled agent names bypass the human-task claim barrier","location":"src/bus/task.ts:1164","evidence":"The force guard excludes HUMAN_CLAIMANTS, while src/cli/bus.ts:684-695 lets any caller supply `--agent human` or `--agent user`. Thus claimTask does not refuse every human-exempt task lacking force, and the guard is trivially bypassable.","fix":"Remove the claimant-name exemption. Amend the FR-010 allowlist to update src/bus/multica/poll.ts so its deliberate human synchronization calls claimTask with `{force:true}` explicitly."}],"rejected_as_locked":["D-11 known-entities-only state writes; unknown humans remain in the attention lane","Tier-1 SequenceMatcher threshold is strictly greater than 0.75","The Gmail list API remains capped at 50 without pagination; per-day truncation and returned list order are accepted","No triviality gate before extraction","Extraction summary is not quote-gated","Grounded attacker-authored quotes from the message body survive by design","The records lane intentionally excludes bus comms-filter"]}
